step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_23", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_25", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_27", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_29", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "I could not verify a time-respecting cascade from 1330 to 361 in the requested window. There are no direct events between 1330 and 361 (step_03). Both nodes have relatively few events overall (step_06). 1330\u2019s outgoing neighbors and 361\u2019s incoming neighbors were inspected (steps_04, _07), and direct two-hop static links from 1330\u2192neighbor\u2192361 were not found for the checked neighbors (steps_11\u201330). Node 28 is highly active and is an in-neighbor of 361 (step_09) but 1330 has no edge to 28 (step_10), so popular-node confounding does not establish a time-respecting chain. Crucially, I did not obtain timestamped event sequences showing a temporally ordered chain with gaps \u2264600, so the available temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude a genuine cascade within [4765,43165]."}, "raw_final_response": "{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_88df71e2\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1330, 361],\n  \"window\": [4765, 43165],\n  \"confidence\": 0.60,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_29\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"I could not verify a time-respecting cascade from 1330 to 361 in the requested window. There are no direct events between 1330 and 361 (step_03). Both nodes have relatively few events overall (step_06). 1330\u2019s outgoing neighbors and 361\u2019s incoming neighbors were inspected (steps_04, _07), and direct two-hop static links from 1330\u2192neighbor\u2192361 were not found for the checked neighbors (steps_11\u201330). Node 28 is highly active and is an in-neighbor of 361 (step_09) but 1330 has no edge to 28 (step_10), so popular-node confounding does not establish a time-respecting chain. Crucially, I did not obtain timestamped event sequences showing a temporally ordered chain with gaps \u2264600, so the available temporal evidence is insufficient to conclude a genuine cascade within [4765,43165].\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 137872, "total_output_tokens": 4531, "total_tokens": 142403, "total_latency_ms": 69938, "llm_calls": 31, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}